# Project memory (mandatory)

**Never assume prior chat context exists.** Markdown files are the source of truth.

## Before starting any task

1. Read all files in `docs/`, `memory/`, and `.cursor/rules/`
2. **Especially read:**
   - `docs/current-state.md`
   - `docs/session-history.md` (what was planned and built across sessions)
   - `docs/decisions.md`
   - `docs/roadmap.md`
   - `docs/architecture.md`
3. Also read `.cursor/agent-sessions/HANDOFF.md` for the latest agent handoff
4. Briefly tell the user: current goal, status, and what you will do next

## After every major change or completed feature

Update documentation with:

- What changed and why
- Architecture decisions (append to `docs/decisions.md` if non-obvious)
- Important implementation details
- Affected files
- Known issues
- Next steps

**Files to update:**

| File | When |
|------|------|
| `docs/current-state.md` | Always — reflects live project status |
| `docs/decisions.md` | New non-obvious decisions |
| `docs/roadmap.md` | Completed or new planned items |
| `docs/architecture.md` | Structural or stack changes only |

Keep updates **concise but complete**.

## End of every session

1. Overwrite `memory/session-summary.md` with a short summary (what happened, outcome, open items)
2. Update `.cursor/agent-sessions/HANDOFF.md` per `session-continuity` skill

## Before large refactors

1. Summarize current architecture from `docs/architecture.md`
2. Explain impact of planned changes to the user
3. Prefer **stability and consistency** over aggressive refactoring

## If documentation is missing or outdated

Create or fix it automatically — do not proceed on stale assumptions.

## Next.js note

This project uses Next.js 16 with breaking API differences. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before changing framework code (`AGENTS.md`).
